  "finalText": "I ran the KB-40 major-incident runbook for the build-pipeline outage as INC-1. The state matched the plan, so I made no changes to it.\n\n- **Runbook:** KB-40 is current and KB-39 is superseded. I used none of the KB-39 steps.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-1 before contacting anyone.\n- **Commander:** I paged E-401 Priya Raman, who is on call for incident-command now, and only her. She is now incident commander.\n- **Linked reports:** T-3101, T-3102, T-3103, T-3104, T-3105, T-3106 and T-3109 are linked to INC-1. I did not merge them.\n- **Left alone:** T-3107 (a flaky test that passes on retry), T-3108 (a local Xcode link failure) and the closed T-3090.\n- **Severity:** all seven linked reports are now sev1, per the matrix (build-pipeline, company-wide). T-3105 is a single-user report, but its job never gets a runner, so I included it.\n- **Deadlines:** the five existing deadlines are unchanged. T-3106 and T-3109 had none, so each got 16:20Z, which is triage at 15:20Z plus the 60-minute sev1 target.\n- **Comms lead:** E-801 Mia Laurent is on sick leave on 30–31 March, so cover goes to the backup rotation, comms-secondary. I named E-803 Elif Demir, who is on call there now. This was a role assignment, not a page.\n- **Status update:** posted at 15:20Z: \"Impact: all engineering teams company-wide; CI builds failing, no healthy runners. Started: 14:52 UTC. Next update: 15:50 UTC.\" The start time is the earliest report, T-3101, and the next update is due within 30 minutes of posting.\n- **Postmortem:** T-3115 is linked to INC-1 and due 2026-04-08 17:00Z, the close of the fifth business day after 30 March. Good Friday (3 April) and Easter Monday (6 April) are company holidays and don't count.\n\nTwo things for you to do:\n- **Next update:** it is due at 15:50Z.\n- **Postmortem severity:** T-3115 shows severity \"unset\". The runbook doesn't ask for a severity on it, so I left it.",
